# Architecture source of truth

`architecture/` is mandatory project context. Keep it accurate in the same turn as every relevant code change. A new Cursor session with no chat history must understand Flexis from these files alone.

## After every change

If you add, rename, move, or delete a module, route, screen, API, entity, auth path, env var, or convention — update the matching architecture file before you finish. Do not defer. Do not describe systems that are not in the code.

## Where to write (do not collapse into one file)

- `architecture/README.md` — index; update when you add an architecture file
- `architecture/overview.md` — product, system context, tech stack, repo layout
- `architecture/conventions.md` — naming, errors, env, shared patterns
- `architecture/frontend/` — overview, structure, routing, state, UI
- `architecture/backend/` — overview, structure, API, data, security
- `architecture/decisions/` — one ADR file per significant decision

## File rules

- Current facts only. No plans, speculation, or chat recap.
- Unused section: a single `None yet.` line — not empty prose.
- Names, paths, and endpoints must match the codebase.
- Prefer a new focused file over growing a file past ~150 lines.
- Do not duplicate the same fact; link to the file that owns it.

## Do not

- Finish a feature with stale architecture
- Put implementation dumps or generated API specs here; summarize and link to code
